    "created_at": "2025-08-26T02:02:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-26T02:02:42Z",
    "body": "So far, this issue has discussed this question:\n\n1. Why do upload filenames exclude the path?\n\nThat is an important question.\n\nBut look closely at the original issue:\n\n> Once the document is $_POSTed, I get the full path anyway!\n\nThis reveals the real question:\n\n2. Why do upload filenames exposed to scripts exclude the path **even though upload filenames in form submissions include the path anyway**?\n\nThe `<input type>` [File Upload state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#file-upload-state-(type=file)) sets the `value` IDL attribute to mode [filename](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-input-value-filename), which requires the string `C:\\fakepath\\` to be prepended to &#8216;the name of the first file in the list of [selected files](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-input-type-file-selected), if any&#8217;. A note links to an example; the example makes it clear that this &#8216;name&#8217; is supposed to exclude the path.\n\nBut filenames seem to have no normative requirements, except for not containing [path components](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-input-file-path), whatever that means (is that equivalent to saying that filenames cannot contain U+005C REVERSE SOLIDUS?).\n\nI did some quick tests with Firefox and a file whose actual name (not path) included U+005C REVERSE SOLIDUS. Firefox did exclude the path but happily included the full filename, including the U+005C REVERSE SOLIDUS, so I&#8217;m very confused about all this.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
